# PCM Architecture — Persistent Combat Model

## Module Map

```
lib/pcm/
  worldStateEngine.ts          ← Singleton SSoT. All world state reads/writes here.
  adjudicationCore.ts          ← AdjudicationCore interface + 3 concrete implementations
  trainingAdjudicationCore.ts  ← Full training resolution (default)
  spectralRefOrchestrator.ts   ← Selects core, runs adjudication, calls REF, wraps in OversightGate
  spectralRefApi.ts            ← SPECTRAL-REF narrator (calls callBedrock)
  accredited-data-layer.ts     ← Preloads accredited Pk Map for in-turn use only
  gnss-adjudication-bridge.ts  ← ONLY permitted GNSS↔PCM connection
  turn-logic.ts                ← Pure helpers: calculateTimeOfDay, calculatePhase, evaluateOutcome
  require-auth.ts              ← requireSpectralAuth() — auth only, no role check yet

lib/moat/
  moatStore.ts                 ← MOAT persistence (spectral_competency_records + training_plans)
  learnerModelEngine.ts        ← ingestTurn() — idempotent per (exercise, turn)
  curriculumEngine.ts          ← Maps competency gaps → training assignments
  ds-route-auth.ts             ← DS scope: resolveSessionDsPlayerId, dsCanAccessLearner, authorizeDsRoute
```

## Exercise Lifecycle (start → process → endpoint)

```
POST /exercises             → createExercise() → spectral_exercises INSERT
POST /exercises/[id]/start  → startExercise()  → status = active
POST /exercises/[id]/orders → submitOrders()   → spectral_orders INSERT (both forces)
POST /exercises/[id]/turn   → advanceTurn()    → adjudication → REF → MOAT → DB update
GET  /exercises/[id]/aar    → AARDocument      → from spectral_aar_documents
```

## advanceTurn() — The Main Pipeline

Order is fixed. Do not reorder steps.

```
1. requireSpectralAuth()               → auth gate (no role check yet — task #82 pending)
2. worldStateEngine.advanceTurn()
   a. preloadAccreditedData()          → AccreditedDataLayer Map (PCM-scoped, never exported)
   b. defaultCore()                    → selects adjudication core:
        SPECTRAL_PCM_STUB_ADJUDICATION=true → placeholderAdjudicationCore
        isOperationsEdition()          → operationalAdjudicationCore
        else                           → trainingAdjudicationCore
   c. core.resolveTurn(worldState, redOrders, blueOrders, seed, ctx)
   d. generateRefNarrative()           → callBedrock (narrator only, NO Pk in message)
   e. wrapInOversightGate()            → OversightGate { requires_ds_approval, proposed_result }
   f. Fog of War filter                → red_sensor_picture / blue_sensor_picture (no raw state)
   g. processMoatAfterTurn()           → MOAT learner model update
   h. worldStateEngine.saveWorldState() → spectral_world_states INSERT + spectral_exercises UPDATE
3. Return AdvanceTurnResponse to client
```

## Adjudication Core Selection

```ts
// lib/pcm/spectralRefOrchestrator.ts — defaultCore()
function defaultCore(): AdjudicationCore {
  if (process.env.SPECTRAL_PCM_STUB_ADJUDICATION === 'true') return placeholderAdjudicationCore
  if (isOperationsEdition()) return operationalAdjudicationCore
  return trainingAdjudicationCore   // ← default for all training deployments
}
```

All three cores share the same `AdjudicationCore` interface — interchangeable without touching WSE:
```ts
interface AdjudicationCore {
  resolveTurn(
    worldState: WorldState,
    redOrders: Order | null,
    blueOrders: Order | null,
    seed: number,
    ctx?: AdjudicationContext
  ): Promise<ResolvedWorldState>
}
```

## Accredited Data Isolation — Critical Rules

```ts
// lib/pcm/accredited-data-layer.ts
// Preloaded once per turn by worldStateEngine — for resolveTurn() ONLY
const layer: Map<string, AccreditedDefeatPkRow> = await preloadAccreditedData(threatIds, defeatSystemIds)
// selectAccreditedPk(row, defenderGroup) → picks pk_rf_jamming_pct | pk_dew_pct | pk_kinetic_pct
```

**NEVER:**
- Pass AccreditedDataLayer to `processMoatAfterTurn()` or any MOAT function
- Pass Pk values to `generateRefNarrative()` or `buildRefUserMessage()`
- Export accredited Pk to client components or API response bodies
- Access `accredited_defeat_pk` table outside `lib/operations/accredited-supplements.ts`

**Accredited data is PCM-scoped and in-turn only. It is destroyed after turn resolution.**

## GNSS–PCM Bridge — Only One Permitted Connection

```ts
// lib/pcm/gnss-adjudication-bridge.ts ← ONLY file allowed to import from lib/gnss/
export function gnssVulnerabilityForPlatform(platformId, deps): GnssVulnerability
export function countGnssDependentThreats(threatIds, deps, activeJamming): number
```

Any future GNSS–PCM coupling MUST go through this file. Direct imports from `lib/gnss/`
into any other `lib/pcm/` file are prohibited.

## MOAT (Learner Model) — One Write Path

```ts
// processMoatAfterTurn() is the ONLY permitted write path to spectral_competency_records
// Called at the end of advanceTurn(), after adjudication, NEVER with Pk values
await processMoatAfterTurn({
  exerciseId,
  turn,
  observation: {
    decision_time_sec,
    context_flags,
    behaviours: extractedBehaviours,   // trainee decisions only — not combat outcomes
  }
})
```

**Direct INSERT to `spectral_competency_records` or `spectral_training_plans` is prohibited.**
TurnObservation contains trainee decisions (what they chose to do), not combat outcomes (what Pk resolved).

## WorldStateEngine — Singleton Pattern

```ts
// lib/pcm/worldStateEngine.ts
// Uses createServiceRoleNodeClient() — service role + WebSocket transport
// Module-level singleton — re-initialised on cold start (stateless between requests)
export const worldStateEngine = new WorldStateEngine()
```

WSE is the only class with access to raw world state. Players receive filtered sensor pictures:
- `red_sensor_picture` — Red detections only
- `blue_sensor_picture` — Blue detections only
- Raw `all_contacts` / `world_state` never sent to client

## Seeded RNG — Deterministic Adjudication

```ts
// lib/pcm/seeded-rng.ts
// hashTurnSeed(exerciseId, turn) → deterministic seed
// Same exercise + turn always produces the same adjudication result
// Critical for AAR replay and automated testing
```

Always use the seeded RNG inside `resolveTurn()`. Never use `Math.random()` directly in
adjudication logic.

## OversightGate — DS Approval Required

```ts
// Every turn result is wrapped before returning to client
interface OversightGate {
  requires_ds_approval: boolean    // true by default
  proposed_result: AdjudicationResult
  ds_approved: boolean
  ds_player_id: string | null
  ds_notes: string | null
}
```

The DS must approve the proposed result before it is committed. `force_advance: true` in the
POST body skips DS approval (for automated test scenarios only).
